  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's start from the very beginning not just how to reverse, but&nbsp;<strong>why it works</strong>&nbsp;the way it does.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-first-understand-the-problem",
      "title": "1. First, Understand the Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You have a linked list going in one direction",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116264-564778596.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You want it to go the other way:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116265-89419603.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<hr style=\"border-width: 1px medium medium; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(224, 224, 224) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none; margin: 24px 0px;\">",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-why-you-can-t-just-swap-values",
      "title": "2. Why You Can't Just Swap Values",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your first instinct might be why not just swap the data inside the nodes? Put 5 where 1 is, put 4 where 2 is, and so on.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116265-14290634.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116265-14290634.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116265-14290634.png",
          "alt": "Why You Can't Just Swap Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This works for simple cases but falls apart in real interviews. Why?",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Nodes might store complex objects, not just integers",
            "Swapping data is considered cheating the actual structure hasn't changed",
            "The real skill being tested is&nbsp;<strong>pointer manipulation</strong>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The correct approach is to&nbsp;<strong>flip the pointers themselves</strong>, not touch the data at all.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-why-flipping-pointers-is-tricky",
      "title": "3. Why Flipping Pointers is Tricky",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's say you naively try to reverse the first pointer:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We start with the original list:<br>[1] → [2] → [3] → [4] → [5] → null.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If you change the first node so that it points to null, like&nbsp;<code>[1] → null</code>, the connection between 1 and 2 is broken. Once this link is removed, there is no way to reach node 2 from the head anymore.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Even though nodes 2, 3, 4, and 5 still exist in memory, no pointer is pointing to them, so they become unreachable. In a linked list, losing a connection like this means you effectively lose access to the entire remaining part of the list.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The moment you redirect a pointer, you&nbsp;<strong>sever your connection</strong>&nbsp;to the rest of the list. This is the core challenge of reversal.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The solution?&nbsp;<strong>Save the next node before you break the link.</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-the-three-pointer-technique",
      "title": "3. The Three Pointer Technique",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To reverse safely, you maintain three pointers at all times:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116265-235473890.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Think of it like this you're walking through the list with three fingers on three consecutive nodes. At each step you flip the middle one, then all three fingers slide one position forward.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We start with two pointers:&nbsp;<strong>prev</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>curr</strong>. Initially,&nbsp;<strong>prev is null</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>curr points to the first node [1]</strong>&nbsp;in the list:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116266-181303390.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The reason&nbsp;<strong>prev starts as null</strong>&nbsp;is important. When we reverse the list, the first node [1] will eventually become the&nbsp;<strong>last node</strong>, and the last node must point to&nbsp;<strong>null</strong>. By setting prev to null from the beginning, we ensure that when [1] is reversed, it will correctly point to null.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Walking Through Every Single Step",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's go through this slowly, one step at a time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 1: Process node [1]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116266-214680331.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We start with&nbsp;<code>prev = null</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code>curr = [1]</code>.<br>First, we&nbsp;<strong>save next = [2]</strong>&nbsp;so we don’t lose the rest of the list.<br>Then we&nbsp;<strong>reverse the link</strong>:&nbsp;<code>[1] → null</code>.<br>Now move pointers:&nbsp;<code>prev = [1]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [2]</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 2: Process node [2]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116267-317986642.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now&nbsp;<code>prev = [1]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [2]</code>.<br>Save&nbsp;<code>next = [3]</code>.<br>Reverse link:&nbsp;<code>[2] → [1]</code>.<br>Move pointers:&nbsp;<code>prev = [2]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [3]</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 3: Process node [3]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116557-936566059.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Now&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">prev = [2]</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">,&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">curr = [3]</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Save&nbsp;<code>next = [4]</code>.<br>Reverse link:&nbsp;<code>[3] → [2]</code>.<br>Move pointers:&nbsp;<code>prev = [3]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [4]</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 4: Process node [4]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116557-409064750.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now&nbsp;<code>prev = [3]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [4]</code>.<br>Save&nbsp;<code>next = [5]</code>.<br>Reverse link:&nbsp;<code>[4] → [3]</code>.<br>Move pointers:&nbsp;<code>prev = [4]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [5]</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 5: Process node [5]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116558-632273096.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now&nbsp;<code>prev = [4]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = [5]</code>.<br>Save&nbsp;<code>next = null</code>.<br>Reverse link:&nbsp;<code>[5] → [4]</code>.<br>Move pointers:&nbsp;<code>prev = [5]</code>,&nbsp;<code>curr = null</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Final Step: Update Head",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116558-449849573.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now&nbsp;<code>curr = null</code>, so we stop.<br><code>prev</code>&nbsp;is at&nbsp;<code>[5]</code>, which is the new head.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Update:&nbsp;<code>head = prev</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Final List",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-862653620.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Summary:</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We reverse the linked list using three pointers:&nbsp;<strong>prev, curr, and next</strong>. Initially,&nbsp;<code>prev = null</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code>curr</code>&nbsp;points to the first node&nbsp;<code>[1]</code>. At each step, we carefully reverse one link while making sure we don’t lose the rest of the list.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For every node, the first step is to&nbsp;<strong>save the next node</strong>&nbsp;(<code>next = curr.next</code>) so we don’t lose access to the remaining list. Then we&nbsp;<strong>reverse the current node’s pointer</strong>&nbsp;by making&nbsp;<code>curr.next = prev</code>. This flips the direction of the link. After that, we&nbsp;<strong>move both pointers forward</strong>&nbsp;<code>prev</code>&nbsp;moves to the current node, and&nbsp;<code>curr</code>&nbsp;moves to the saved next node.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "As we repeat this process, the list gradually gets reversed: first&nbsp;<code>[1]</code>&nbsp;points to null, then&nbsp;<code>[2]</code>&nbsp;points to&nbsp;<code>[1]</code>, then&nbsp;<code>[3]</code>&nbsp;points to&nbsp;<code>[2]</code>, and so on. Step by step, the reversed portion grows on the left, while the remaining list shrinks on the right.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Eventually,&nbsp;<code>curr</code>&nbsp;becomes null, which means we’ve processed all nodes. At this point,&nbsp;<code>prev</code>&nbsp;is pointing to the last processed node which is the&nbsp;<strong>new head of the reversed list</strong>. So we update&nbsp;<code>head = prev</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "Node prev = null;\nNode curr = head;\nNode next = null;\n\nwhile (curr != null) {\n\n    next = curr.next;    // 1. save next node\n    curr.next = prev;    // 2. flip the pointer\n    prev = curr;         // 3. slide prev forward\n    curr = next;         // 4. slide curr forward\n\n}\n\nhead = prev;             // prev is the new head"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<code>next = curr.next</code>&nbsp;→ save next node before breaking the link",
            "<code>curr.next = prev</code>&nbsp;→ reverse the current node’s pointer",
            "<code>prev = curr</code>&nbsp;→ move prev forward",
            "<code>curr = next</code>&nbsp;→ move curr to next node",
            "<code>head = prev</code>&nbsp;→ update head to new front"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Time complexity: O(n)&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">every node is visited exactly once.</span><br><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Space complexity: O(1)&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">only three extra pointers, no new nodes created.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-common-mistakes-beginners-make",
      "title": "4. Common Mistakes Beginners Make",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p><strong>Golden Rule:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Follow the exact order&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">→</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">save → flip → move → repeat → update head</strong></p>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Mistake 1: Flipping before saving next",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "If you reverse the pointer&nbsp;<strong>before saving next</strong>, you lose the rest of the list",
            "Always&nbsp;<strong>save next first</strong>, then flip the pointer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Rule:&nbsp;<strong>Save → then flip</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Mistake 2 : Forgetting to update HEAD",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "After the loop ends, head still points to the old first node",
            "But that node now points to null → rest of the list is lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Always set&nbsp;<strong>head = prev</strong>&nbsp;at the end",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Mistake 3: Not initializing prev to null",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "If prev is not null initially, the last node will point to the wrong place",
            "This corrupts the list structure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Always start with&nbsp;<strong>prev = null</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    }
